  "instruction_steps": [
    {
      "step_number": 1,
      "instruction": "Heat the oven to 200C/180C fan/gas 6. Bash the garlic, sage, lemon zest, salt and pepper together using a pestle and mortar until the mixture becomes a paste. Stir in the oil, then spread the mixture over the pork shoulder, avoiding the skin on top. Score the skin using a sharp knife, then rub a large pinch of salt into the skin. Tie the pork together using kitchen string.",
      "temperature": {
        "value": 200,
        "unit": "celsius"
      },
      "ingredients_used": [
        "95d0f946-3adf-544b-95b3-f1595b670005",
        "9710e766-5250-5544-8b75-0eb73fc726a8",
        "bb135420-f944-502a-bc61-013bcf398c4f",
        "90e80a07-1ba7-51c4-bed8-6bc1e90ed226"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 2,
      "instruction": "Line a large baking tray with a double layer of foil and put the pork on top, skin-side up. Bring the sides of the foil up around the pork to create a parcel, then pour the wine into the tray around the sides. Transfer to the oven and reduce the temperature to 140C/120C fan/gas 1. Roast for 4-5 hrs, or until a meat thermometer inserted into the thickest part of the pork reads 70C.",
      "timer_seconds": 18000,
      "temperature": {
        "value": 140,
        "unit": "celsius"
      },
      "ingredients_used": [
        "8d3581d8-a383-572f-8417-8a2b0ee32c04"
      ]
    },
    {
      "step_number": 3,
      "instruction": "Turn the oven up to 240C/220C fan/gas 9. Carefully spoon the pork roasting juices from the pan into a saucepan and cook over a medium heat for 10-15 mins, or until reduced by a third. Season to taste.",
      "timer_seconds": 900,
      "temperature": {
        "value": 240,
        "unit": "celsius"
      }
    },
    {
      "step_number": 4,
      "instruction": "Meanwhile, arrange the foil around the meat so only the skin is exposed, then return to the oven for 10-15 mins until the skin is puffed up and browned all over. Leave to rest for 20 mins before slicing. Serve with the sauce drizzled over."
    }
  ],
